<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Evpaty Kolovrat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Yevpaty Kolovrat</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Evpaty Kolovrat is a legendary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryazan">Ryazan</a> noble whose deeds are told in the Tale of the Destruction of Ryazan by Batu, a work of Old Russian literature. Returning from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chernigov">Chernigov</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> destroyed Ryazan in December 1237, he is said to have gathered some 1,700 men and attacked Batu's army, fighting on until he was killed. He became a Russian folk hero.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/evpaty-kolovrat.jpg" alt="Evpaty Kolovrat" width="320" height="296" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Коржев Иван · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Korzhev_Ivan._Evpatiy._%D0%9A%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B6%D0%B5%D0%B2_%D0%98._%D0%95%D0%B2%D0%BF%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%9A%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B2%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%82,_2009,_%D0%BB%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%8C%D0%B5%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%B9_%D0%BA%D0%B0%D0%BC%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8C_%D1%82%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%BA%D0%B0_%D0%BF%D0%BE%D0%B4_%D0%B1%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B7%D1%83_%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9_%D0%BC%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BB%D0%BB,_83%D1%8590%D1%8567%D1%81%D0%BC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
